<title>PERU: LatAm to consume 9 pct more copper in 5 yrs -- group.</title>
<headline>LatAm to consume 9 pct more copper in 5 yrs -- group.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Latin American group for promoting copper usage said Thursday consumption of the red metal in the region would increase by 50,000 tonnes a year to 600,000 tonnes annually by 2000.</p>
<p>&quot;Through promotional work we reckon during the next five years consumption of copper in the region will increase 50,000 tonnes,&quot; said Peter Lowick-Russell, coordinator for Copper Promotional Centers, known as Procobre.</p>
<p>The group has offices in Chile, Brazil, Mexico, Argentina and Peru, which together produce 40 percent of the world's copper, according to Procobre.</p>
<p>--Claudia Guillen, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
